  "question": {
    "text": "A body of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> starts moving from rest at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, in a circular path of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. Its kinetic energy varies as a function of times as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>KE</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> Joules, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in seconds. Then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
